  "findings": [
    "OER art. 11.3 fixes ten 6 EC units in year one. The two zero-credit units and associated grade gates are recorded separately. Article 12.1 confirms at least 30 EC in the first semester of year three and sets the approval and level conditions.",
    "The official revision pp. 1–2 and 4–6 specifies six required second-year courses and four choice slots. Period two is Genomics or Qualitative Research, and period four is Anatomy and Physiology 2 or System Transformation. Year three has a biomedical or societal project, preparatory applied methods for the societal project and final Science Communication. The chart and descriptions give no weights for these components.",
    "The annual catalogue currently gives later-year credits for outgoing specialisations. OER art. 9.1 names AB_1195 and AB_1196 and references outgoing-route prerequisites, so the 42 EC gate and older project rules cannot be transferred to the redesigned project without confirmation. The faculty overview explicitly notes that some revised courses are absent from the guide. Searches for later cohort editions and exact revised course names found no usable official credit and progression table."
  ],
